            <ArticleTitle>The safety of complete mesocolic excision once again confirmed.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/codi.13967</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We would like to commend Bernhoff and colleagues (1) for publishing further evidence supporting complete mesocolic excision (CME) as a safe approach in colon cancer surgery. They report no increased risk of 30-day mortality or reoperation after right-sided CME in a nested case-control study. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
